{
  "uid": "marketplace-health",
  "title": "Marketplace — service health",
  "description": "Built from the register's P2.1/P2.2 entries. Metrics answer 'is the system healthy'; logs answer 'for whom' — which is why no panel here is broken down by tenant and every log line is.",
  "tags": [
    "marketplace"
  ],
  "timezone": "Europe/Moscow",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 2,
  "refresh": "30s",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-6h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "editable": true,
  "panels": [
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Critical alarms — a new seller's history is not arriving",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 1
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Stuck backfill lanes",
      "description": "Lanes that claim to be running and have stopped moving, fleet-wide. Anything above zero means a seller's history has stopped arriving and nothing else in the system will say so. Which seller is in the logs below — metrics here carry no tenant.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "marketplace-prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1,
        "w": 5,
        "h": 7
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "marketplace-prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "backfill_lanes_stalled or vector(0)",
          "legendFormat": "stuck",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Deaths and restarts, by lane",
      "description": "Read as a pair. Failures rising while restarts follow them and the stuck count returns to zero is the watchdog healing the system. Restarts rising while the stuck count stays up is the restart NOT working — a poisoned cursor or a rejected token — and that is the one worth interrupting someone for.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "marketplace-prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 5,
        "y": 1,
        "w": 10,
        "h": 7
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "marketplace-prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (lane) (increase(backfill_lane_failures_total[15m]))",
          "legendFormat": "died · {{lane}}",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "marketplace-prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (lane) (increase(backfill_lane_restarts_total[15m]))",
          "legendFormat": "restarted · {{lane}}",
          "refId": "B"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 10
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "logs",
      "title": "Which seller, and why — backfill log lines",
      "description": "The tenant half of the alarm. A metric may not name a workspace, so the alert says THAT a lane is stuck and this says WHOSE: every line carries workspace_id, the lane and its cursor.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "marketplace-loki"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 15,
        "y": 1,
        "w": 9,
        "h": 7
      },
      "options": {
        "showTime": true,
        "wrapLogMessage": true,
        "sortOrder": "Descending",
        "enableLogDetails": true
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "loki",
            "uid": "marketplace-loki"
          },
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "{job=\"marketplace\"} |= \"backfill\""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 101,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Service health — is it up, and is it answering",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 8,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 1
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 102,
      "title": "Dependencies",
      "type": "stat",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "marketplace-prometheus"
      },
      "description": "The same probe /healthz reports to UptimeRobot, refreshed by the scrape itself so it exists whether or not anything external is polling. min across instances: down anywhere is down.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 9,
        "w": 6,
        "h": 5
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "marketplace-prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "min by (dependency) (dependency_up)",
          "legendFormat": "{{dependency}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "mappings": [
            {
              "type": "value",
              "options": {
                "0": {
                  "text": "DOWN",
                  "color": "red",
                  "index": 0
                },
                "1": {
                  "text": "up",
                  "color": "green",
                  "index": 1
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 103,
      "title": "Requests per second by status",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "marketplace-prometheus"
      },
      "description": "Exact status codes rather than 2xx/4xx buckets: 401, 403 and 429 mean different things and are alerted on separately.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 6,
        "y": 9,
        "w": 10,
        "h": 5
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "marketplace-prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (status) (rate(http_requests_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{status}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps",
          "custom": {}
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 104,
      "title": "Latency p95 by route",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "marketplace-prometheus"
      },
      "description": "Unmatched paths are grouped as handler=\"none\" — a URL scanner cannot create a series per URL it tries.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 16,
        "y": 9,
        "w": 8,
        "h": 5
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "marketplace-prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le, handler) (rate(http_request_duration_seconds_bucket[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "{{handler}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "custom": {}
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 105,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "WildBerries — the dependency that fails least visibly",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 14,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 1
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 106,
      "title": "WB calls per second by outcome",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "marketplace-prometheus"
      },
      "description": "transport_error and rate_blocked are counted alongside HTTP statuses because they are how WB actually fails: an over-budget request is answered by holding the connection open, not with a 429.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 15,
        "w": 8,
        "h": 6
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "marketplace-prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (status) (rate(wb_api_requests_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{status}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps",
          "custom": {}
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 107,
      "title": "Rate budget WB says is left",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "marketplace-prometheus"
      },
      "description": "Empty until a harvest calls a PACED surface (analytics, marketplace). The leading indicator: it reaches zero while there is still time to react.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 8,
        "y": 15,
        "w": 8,
        "h": 6
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "marketplace-prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "wb_rate_limit_quota_remaining",
          "legendFormat": "{{surface}} {{endpoint}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "custom": {}
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 108,
      "title": "Seconds spent waiting on the rate gate",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "marketplace-prometheus"
      },
      "description": "Pacing pressure. Zero is the healthy reading — it only rises when WB's bucket is empty and we are queueing rather than sending.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 16,
        "y": 15,
        "w": 8,
        "h": 6
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "marketplace-prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (surface) (rate(wb_rate_limit_wait_seconds_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{surface}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "custom": {}
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 109,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Harvests — did the work happen, and did it produce anything",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 21,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 1
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 110,
      "title": "Rows ingested per source",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "marketplace-prometheus"
      },
      "description": "The panel that would have shown the 2026-07-30 incident on day one: tasks reporting SUCCESS while every funnel source silently returned nothing. Populated by the nightly pass (06:00 MSK), the interactive «Обновить», and the hourly finreports walk — so it is legitimately empty between runs.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 22,
        "w": 8,
        "h": 6
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "marketplace-prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (source) (increase(harvest_rows_processed_total[1h]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{source}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "custom": {}
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 111,
      "title": "Partial harvests (a source withheld data)",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "marketplace-prometheus"
      },
      "description": "A partial harvest is tolerated by design so one dead surface does not lose the run — which is exactly why it needs counting. Empty is the good reading.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 8,
        "y": 22,
        "w": 8,
        "h": 6
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "marketplace-prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (harvest, source) (increase(harvest_partial_total[1h]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{harvest}} / {{source}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "custom": {}
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 112,
      "title": "Harvest duration p95",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "marketplace-prometheus"
      },
      "description": "",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 16,
        "y": 22,
        "w": 8,
        "h": 6
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "marketplace-prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le, harvest) (rate(harvest_duration_seconds_bucket[30m])))",
          "legendFormat": "{{harvest}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "custom": {}
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 113,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Queues and pools — saturation",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 28,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 1
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 114,
      "title": "Celery queue depth",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "marketplace-prometheus"
      },
      "description": "Read from Redis with LLEN at scrape time, never derived from enqueue/dequeue counters. `unacked` staying high while the queue drains means work is taken and not finishing. Aggregated across instances — they read one Redis, so summing would multiply one queue by the number of scrapers.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 29,
        "w": 8,
        "h": 6
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "marketplace-prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "max by (queue_name) (celery_queue_length)",
          "legendFormat": "{{queue_name}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "custom": {}
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 115,
      "title": "Task rate by state",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "marketplace-prometheus"
      },
      "description": "",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 8,
        "y": 29,
        "w": 8,
        "h": 6
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "marketplace-prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (state) (rate(celery_tasks_total[10m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{state}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops",
          "custom": {}
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 116,
      "title": "Postgres pool",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "marketplace-prometheus"
      },
      "description": "Each API instance and the worker keep their own pool, so these stay per-instance: collapsing them would hide an exhausted pool behind two idle ones. Exhaustion has happened here — leaked `idle in transaction` connections held every slot for 22 hours.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 16,
        "y": 29,
        "w": 8,
        "h": 6
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "marketplace-prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "postgres_pool_connections_used",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}} used",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "marketplace-prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "postgres_pool_connections_free",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}} free",
          "refId": "B"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "marketplace-prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "postgres_pool_connections_overflow",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}} overflow",
          "refId": "C"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "custom": {}
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 117,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Security — controls, counted where they fire",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 35,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 1
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 118,
      "title": "RLS violations (24h)",
      "type": "stat",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "marketplace-prometheus"
      },
      "description": "Should read 0 forever. One increment means a code path reached tenant data without passing the tenancy choke point — the exact defect row-level security was installed to catch. Shows 0 rather than \"No data\" when the counter has never fired, because on a security panel those two must not look alike.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 36,
        "w": 6,
        "h": 5
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "marketplace-prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum(increase(security_rls_violations_total[24h])) or vector(0)",
          "legendFormat": "24h",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 119,
      "title": "Degraded security controls",
      "type": "stat",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "marketplace-prometheus"
      },
      "description": "1 while a control runs its fail-open fallback (register P1.2). max across instances: degraded anywhere is degraded. Two at once is the correlated failure the ledger exists to surface.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 6,
        "y": 36,
        "w": 6,
        "h": 5
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "marketplace-prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "max by (control) (security_degraded_controls)",
          "legendFormat": "{{control}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 120,
      "title": "Authentication failures by reason",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "marketplace-prometheus"
      },
      "description": "No account or address is a label — the count is the alert, the identity is in the logs. Empty until a login is refused.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 12,
        "y": 36,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 5
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "marketplace-prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (reason) (rate(security_auth_failures_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{reason}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops",
          "custom": {}
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 121,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Logs",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 41,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 1
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 122,
      "type": "logs",
      "title": "Errors and warnings, all containers",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "marketplace-loki"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 42,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 10
      },
      "description": "Filters on `detected_level`, which Loki derives for EVERY line, rather than on our own `level` label. That is not a preference: `level` exists only on lines the application emits as JSON, so a query using it structurally excludes Postgres, Redis and nginx — it could never show a Postgres FATAL. Everything identifying WHOSE request a line belongs to (trace_id, workspace_id, user_id) is inside the JSON: filter with `| json | workspace_id=\"...\"`. Those are deliberately not labels — a trace_id label would be one Loki stream per request.",
      "options": {
        "showTime": true,
        "wrapLogMessage": true,
        "sortOrder": "Descending",
        "enableLogDetails": true
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "loki",
            "uid": "marketplace-loki"
          },
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "{job=\"marketplace\"} | detected_level =~ \"error|warn|critical|fatal\""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 123,
      "type": "logs",
      "title": "Everything, all containers (live)",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "marketplace-loki"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 52,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 12
      },
      "description": "Unfiltered, and it earns its space by answering a question the panel above cannot: is the log pipeline working, or is there simply nothing wrong? An errors-only panel reads identically in both cases, which is how an 'everything is fine' dashboard and a broken shipper look the same.",
      "options": {
        "showTime": true,
        "wrapLogMessage": true,
        "sortOrder": "Descending",
        "enableLogDetails": true
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "loki",
            "uid": "marketplace-loki"
          },
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "{job=\"marketplace\"}"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
